**Verdict:** The $861 saved by skipping D-IF or D-FL funds a $600–$800 setting upgrade — pavé prongs, platinum metal, or a halo band. The stone looks identical. The ring looks dramatically better. Skip Flawless.

## Rule 5 — Hold L:W Between 1.90 and 2.00

Length-to-width ratio decides the silhouette at 1.5ct. The sweet spot is **1.90 to 2.00** for most buyers.

**Narrower than 1.90 (closer to 1.70–1.85):** Shorter and wider silhouette. Amplifies bow-tie because the pavilion facets have less distance to spread out. The dark zone across the center of the stone looks concentrated and heavy. Avoid at 1.5ct.

**1.90 to 2.00 (the sweet spot):** Classic marquise silhouette. Bow-tie spreads evenly across a longer facet pattern. Face-up measures 11.5–12.0 × 6.0–6.3 mm. Reads as "a serious engagement ring stone" without feeling thin.

**Wider than 2.00 (up to 2.10):** Elongated silhouette. Thins the stone and amplifies length over width. Can read as dramatic on size 4–6 fingers, delicate on size 7+. Still inside the acceptable range at 1.5ct.

**Above 2.10:** Bow-tie moves to the tips of the stone and gets harder to control. Reserved for buyers who specifically want the ultra-elongated look. Full detail in our [marquise length to width ratio guide](/marquise-diamond-length-to-width-ratio).

<table class="dc-custom-table"><thead><tr><th>L:W Ratio</th><th>Face-Up at 1.5ct</th><th>Bow-Tie Risk</th><th>What this means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>1.75</strong></td><td>11.3 × 6.5 mm</td><td>High</td><td>Short and wide. Bow-tie concentrates. Avoid.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>1.90</strong></td><td>11.7 × 6.2 mm</td><td>Medium</td><td>Entry to the sweet spot. Classic silhouette.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>2.00</strong></td><td>12.0 × 6.0 mm</td><td>Low</td><td>Our pick. Standard marquise ratio.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>2.10</strong></td><td>12.3 × 5.9 mm</td><td>Low</td><td>Elongated classic. Dramatic on small fingers.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>2.25</strong></td><td>13.0 × 5.8 mm</td><td>Medium (tip bow-tie)</td><td>Ultra-elongated. Only for specific aesthetic preference.</td></tr></tbody></table>

**Verdict:** 2.00 L:W is the honest sweet spot at 1.5ct — standard silhouette, lowest bow-tie risk, maximum perceived size. 1.90 and 2.10 are both acceptable. Anything outside 1.85–2.15 introduces visible risk at this carat tier.

> **"The L:W ratio is the one spec I check before anything else at 1.5ct. A stone with great colour and clarity but 1.75 L:W will look worse on the hand than a lower-grade stone at 2.00 L:W. Shape wins over spec at this size."** — Farzana Hasan, GIA Diamond Expert

