## How to Verify a 1.5 Carat Marquise Before You Buy

Three checks every stone must pass before you add to cart.

**Check 1 — The certificate measurements.** For a 1.5ct marquise at 2.00 L:W, measurements should read close to 12.0 × 6.0 × 3.7 mm. If length is below 11.6 mm, the stone is cut deep and wasting carat weight below the girdle. More in our [marquise ideal proportions guide](/marquise-cut-diamond-ideal-proportions).

**Check 2 — The HD video for bow-tie severity.** Open the 360° HD video on the retailer listing. Look at the center of the stone face-up. A faint shadow is normal. A hard dark band is the Bow-Tie Amplifier at work — walk away. Full grading in our [marquise bow-tie guide](/marquise-diamond-bow-tie).

**Check 3 — L:W ratio inside 1.90–2.00.** Divide the length measurement by the width measurement. If the result is below 1.90 or above 2.10, Rule 5 flags the stone as off-spec. Reject.

I run these three checks on every 1.5ct marquise before I quote a client. The 5-rule framework only pays off if the stone itself passes these three physical checks first.

